          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Avoid being the last player with cards in phase 2; the last player left with cards is the loser (the skitgubbe).',
          gameplay: "Two phases. Phase 1: Two-player tricks; player to dealer's left leads, next player plays; higher card wins; no follow suit; after playing, each draws from stock to keep three cards. Equal cards (stunsa): cards stay, both draw, same leader leads again. Option: turn up top card of stock and play it. Last card of stock sets trump for phase 2. Phase 2: Player who drew trump leads; must beat previous card (higher same suit or any trump) or pick it up; trick complete when as many cards as active players; completer leads next or player to left if out.",
          keyRules: [
            'Phase 1: Two-card tricks, higher rank wins, draw from stock after playing.',
            'Phase 2: Beat or pick up; follow suit when beating; trump beats non-trump.',
            'Last card of stock determines trump; holder leads phase 2.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "In Phase 1, throw away your low cards (Trash). Keep your Aces and 10s. Do not win tricks that contain low cards unless you have to (Phase 1 tricks go into your hand for Phase 2? Yes! You collect the trick). So, you want to win tricks with high cards inside them. Losing a trick means you don't get the cards. But you want high cards. So win big tricks.",
          intermediate: 'Counting Suits: In Phase 2, you must follow suit. If you have the only Spade left (the Ace), hold it until someone leads Spades, then crush them. If you have small cards in Phase 2, try to sneak them out early or on a new lead.',
          advanced: "The 'Sacrifice': Sometimes in Phase 1, you let an opponent win a trick full of Queens if it means you can save your Ace for a trick full of Aces/Kings later. The quality of your Phase 2 hand is everything.",
          tips: [
            "Don't hoard one suit in Phase 1—diversity helps in Phase 2.",
            'The last trick of Phase 1 is crucial for lead control.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
